<section class="sec sec-tint"><div class="wrap faq-wrap"><div class="faq-l reveal"><p class="kicker">Where to start</p><h2>Most claims start with an estimate audit</h2><p>Before anyone demands appraisal, it helps to know exactly where the insurer’s estimate falls short and what the gap is worth. Many disputes close at that stage.</p><a class="btn btn-dark" href="/appraisal-practice/estimate-audit/">About estimate audits <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div><div class="reveal"><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can I hire you for just one step?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Plenty of owners start with an estimate audit and decide later whether to demand appraisal.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you take commercial and HOA claims?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes — houses, condos, rentals, multifamily, retail, office, churches and association-owned buildings.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work outside the big cities?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We cover all 88 Ohio counties, rural townships included.</p></div></details></div></div></div></section>
